   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Direct pronouns",
     "texto": [
      "They replace the direct object (the person or thing the action is done to): **lo** (him / it, masculine singular), **la** (her / it, feminine singular), **li** (them, masculine plural), **le** (them, feminine plural).",
      "They usually go **before the conjugated verb**: **Lo conosco** (I know him / it); **La chiamo** (I call her / it); **Li invito** (I invite them); **Le ascolto** (I listen to them)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "First and second person pronouns",
     "texto": [
      "**mi** (me), **ti** (you), **ci** (us), **vi** (you, plural): **Mi conosci?** (do you know me?); **Ti aspetto** (I'm waiting for you)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
